<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<section xml:id="SummaryActivities" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Summary Activity Policies</title>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Purpose</title>

        <p>
            This component of assessment has several purposes:
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <term>Practice.</term> Doing problems outside of class is
                    key to learning mathematics.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <term>Immediate feedback.</term> For the Summary Activity
                    part of the Runestone assignment you are immediately told
                    whether an answer is right or wrong (for most problems) -
                    you don't need to wait for me to grade and return homework.
                </li>

                <li>
                    <term>An opportunity for productive failure.</term> On the
                    checkpoints within the Summary Activity you will have
                    multiple attempts on each problem because it is okay to make
                    mistakes.
                    In fact, making mistakes is a key part of learning.
                    The attempts on each problem are limited though because we
                    want this failure to be productive, that is, we want to
                    learn from our mistakes.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Accessing Runestone</title>

        <p>
            Begin by going to
            <url href="https://landing.runestone.academy">
      https://landing.runestone.academy
    </url>.
        </p>

        <p>
            See Runestone Instructions on Blackboard for further details.
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Completing Summary Activities in Runestone</title>

        <p>
            <ol>
                <li>
                    Follow the assignment link in Blackboard to the appropriate
                    page for the Assignment in Runestone.
                    These are also visible in the Assignments portion of your
                    Runestone Dashboard.
                </li>

                <li>Make sure to answer each question and hit "Submit."</li>
                <li>
                    I will grade the "best" answer out of your attempts and this
                    is what will save with Runestone.
                </li>
            </ol>
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Feedback and Grading</title>

        <p>
            Summary activity assignments are due on Thursdays at 11:59pm.
            Summary activity assignments will count as 15% of your grade.
            These will be graded for correctness.
            If you earn 90% of the points you will get full credit.
            If you earn less than 90% your grade will be scaled appropriately.
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Academic Honesty</title>

        <p>
            You may use your book, your notes, me, your peers, and the math
            center for help on the Summary Activities.
            You may NOT use any other internet resources, including googling
            answers, ChatGPT or any AI.
            It is important for your learning that you do these problems for
            yourself.
            Any instances of academic dishonesty will be reported to the Office
            of Student Conduct and Conflict Resolution.
            Penalties can include failure of an assignment, a 0 on the Summary
            Activity part of your grade, and/or failure of the course.
            Remember I want to help, just email me!
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
</section>